174
00:10:34.481 --> 00:10:36.922
We don't exactly live
in a thriving metropolis.

175
00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.861
Ten minutes at my grandparents'.
and you would disagree.

176
00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:44.991
What am I supposed to do
all summer without you?

177
00:10:46.366 --> 00:10:49.610
- Wait. you're... you're gonna miss me?
- Of course.

178
00:10:49.612 --> 00:10:51.246
You're the only friend I have left.

179
00:10:52.332 --> 00:10:53.374
Come on. that's not true.

180
00:10:55.751 --> 00:10:58.630
Will you write me.
like. old-school letters?

181
00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.507
Yeah. I mean. can I write them
on the computer and print them?

182
00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.260
You may not. And no postcards.

183
00:11:06.261 --> 00:11:10.058
I want handwritten missives filled
with your deepest. darkest secrets.

184
00:11:11.183 --> 00:11:12.434
Are you gonna write me back?

185
00:11:13.352 --> 00:11:14.810
"Dear Helmet.

186
00:11:14.813 --> 00:11:16.978
today. someone smeared
feces on the bathroom wall.

187
00:11:16.981 --> 00:11:18.773
and I got to clean it up.

188
00:11:18.775 --> 00:11:21.093
But there was an
expired box of Milk Duds

189
00:11:21.097 --> 00:11:23.110
that I got to take home for free."

190
00:11:23.111 --> 00:11:25.140
Those are your deepest
and darkest secrets?

191
00:11:26.031 --> 00:11:27.449
Write me. and you'll find out.

192
00:11:30.828 --> 00:11:32.413
Whoa!

193
00:11:33.081 --> 00:11:34.249
I never wrote her.

194
00:11:37.945 --> 00:11:39.169
I just...

195
00:11:41.005 --> 00:11:44.881
Summer gets away from
you. and stuff happens.

196
00:11:44.884 --> 00:11:47.802
And I guess I didn't really think
that she'd be thinking of me.

197
00:11:47.804 --> 00:11:50.727
I mean. I didn't think
I was that important.

198
00:11:51.933 --> 00:11:55.687
And you always think that... you
think that you'll have plenty of time.

199
00:12:00.906 --> 00:12:02.110
I'm sorry.

200
00:12:08.366 --> 00:12:10.156
- What the hell?
- Whatever happened to

201
00:12:10.159 --> 00:12:12.784
"What happens in The Clubhouse
stays in The Clubhouse"?

202
00:12:12.786 --> 00:12:15.068
Not in here. Jesus.

203
00:12:15.071 --> 00:12:18.333
- What the fuck is your problem?
- Somebody's blackmailing me.

204
00:12:20.002 --> 00:12:22.093
If my dad sees that. I'm dead.

205
00:12:22.097 --> 00:12:23.213
Fuck.

206
00:12:24.464 --> 00:12:26.799
Look. you need to
help me shut this down.

207
00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.970
- I need to?
- You owe me.

208
00:12:29.721 --> 00:12:31.906
I don't owe anybody anything. Marcus.

209
00:12:33.348 --> 00:12:35.308
I got a lot of eyes
on me right now. okay?

210
00:12:35.309 --> 00:12:38.110
I can't get involved
in some stripper shit.

211
00:12:38.112 --> 00:12:40.939
- You're already involved. You were there.
- I'm not in the video.

212
00:12:41.649 --> 00:12:42.939
Are you fucking kidding me?

213
00:12:42.942 --> 00:12:46.068
After what I did for you in
court. you can't return the favor?

214
00:12:46.069 --> 00:12:48.695
A favor's only a favor
if someone asks for it.

215
00:12:48.698 --> 00:12:51.110
And I didn't ask you to
drag my name into this shit.

216
00:12:51.112 --> 00:12:52.366
That's on you.

217
00:12:59.415 --> 00:13:02.375
Clay. you've testified today
that Hannah was a victim

218
00:13:02.377 --> 00:13:04.880
